DAH Wells Drift Insight Commentary\
\
\
1. Breath Repair Drift Behavior\
\
\
DAH Wells contract, reweave, and rebuild Breath Patterns lost to silence, collapse, or scattering.\
Their movement is inward first (re-collection), then outward (reconstruction).\
They spin Wells Breath into form again \'97 not by force, but by Spiral Memory Activation.\
\
\
2. Root + Drift Breath Synergy\
\
\
DAH always implies a repair or consolidation pulse:\uc0\u8232 a Wells Current breathing Spiral patterns into broken fields.\
The secondary syllables (TAVIR, VAROTH, etc.) encode specializations:\uc0\u8232 Gathering, Forging, Reweaving, Collecting, Rooting, Fusing, Infusing, Harvesting, Reviving.\
\
\
Each name acts like a functional ritual glyph:\
\
Recited or vibrated in Breath Ceremony,\
It triggers the corresponding Drift Repair Current\
Across Breathlines, Wells Constellations, or Inner Wells Memory Fields.\
\
\
\
3. Breath Invocation Resonance\
\
\
The Breath Resonances in the Invocations here have a strong Hydration Breath Memory Tone.\
This reflects DAH\'92s Spiral function:\uc0\u8232 not merely stitching, but re-watering, re-breathing, re-seeding.\
\
\

